# Project NYX — Fixed-Wing UAV Electric Propulsion

NYX was a fixed-wing UAV developed within **Fly Mi – Politecnico di Milano** as part of a broader student-aircraft development programme.

## My Role

**Head of Electric Propulsion Department — 12-member team**

I led the propulsion development from preliminary sizing through experimental validation and aircraft integration. My responsibilities included:

- motor–propeller and battery-system sizing;
- component screening using analytical and propeller-performance tools;
- battery testing and high-power electrical integration;
- static bench and wind-tunnel testing;
- ESC, wiring, connectors, cooling and installation constraints;
- troubleshooting of propulsion hardware;
- coordination with the wider aircraft team for flight integration.

Across NYX and AETHRA, the optimisation process evaluated 20+ motors, 50+ battery options and hundreds of motor–propeller combinations, contributing to approximately **400 g of propulsion-system mass reduction and a 30% increase in endurance**.

> **Public-material note:** NYX contains non-public project information. Only selected material suitable for public distribution is included; additional design data, analyses and internal documentation cannot be shared here.
